'''Gen.G Esports''' (often abbreviated as '''Gen.G''' and officially short for '''Generation Gaming''', and formerly known as '''<abbr title="Korea + Silicon Valley">KSV</abbr> eSports''') is an [[:category:United States|American]] esports organization.

==Timeline==
{{tabs dynamic
|name1=2019
|name2=2020
|name3=2021
|name4=2024
|This=4

|content1=
* December 6th - '''Gen.G Esports''' enter ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' with the acquisition of [[Cloud9]]'s core, consisting of [[autimatic]], [[daps]], and [[koosta]]. Additionally, [[Cloud9]]'s assistant coach, [[Elmapuddy]], joins as the team's coach. <ref name="CSGO">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/GenG/status/1203011282833567744|title=We are honored to join the CS:GO community and welcome three veteran players as the core of our CS roster|author='''Gen.G Esports'''|date=2019-12-06}}</ref>
* December 9th - '''Gen.G Esports''' acquire [[s0m]] from [[Team Envy]]. <ref name="+s0m">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/GenG/status/1204173880908226562|title=You guessed it!|author='''Gen.G Esports'''|date=2019-12-09}}</ref>
* December 22nd - '''Gen.G Esports''' acquire [[BnTeT]] from [[TYLOO]]. <ref name="+BnTeT">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/GenG/status/1208931482867240961|title=We’re so happy to announce @BnTeTCSGO will join the Gen.G CS:GO roster!|author='''Gen.G Esports'''|date=2019-12-22}}</ref>

|content2=
* September 11th - [[daps]] steps down from the active lineup. <ref name="daps bench">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/GenG/status/1304466148759494657|title=As of today, @daps has stepped down from Gen.G's CSGO roster|author='''Gen.G Esports'''|date=2020-09-11}}</ref>
* September 17th - [[daps]]'s contract expires and he leaves the team. <ref name="-daps">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/daps/status/1307029938571292673|title=Forgot to say this but as of yesterday I am officially contract free for the first time in 5 years|author=[[daps]]|date=2020-09-18}}</ref>
* October 7th - [[s0m]] retires from ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' after being acquired by [[valorant:NRG Esports|NRG Esports' ''VALORANT'' division]]. <ref name="-s0m">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/NRGgg/status/1313894398871175174|title=Oh...looks like NRG Valorant found their duelist|author=[[valorant:NRG Esports|NRG Esports]]|date=2020-10-07}}</ref>

|content3=
* January 21st - [[koosta]] retires from competitive ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' after being transferred to [[valorant:Gen.G Esports|Gen.G Esports's ''VALORANT'' roster]]. <ref name="-koosta">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/geng/status/1352390522283954176|title=You know and love him from our CS:GO team, but now it’s time to #ChangeTheGame|author='''Gen.G Esports'''|date=2021-01-21}}</ref>
* January 24th - [[BnTeT]] is acquired by [[EXTREMUM]] and [[Elmapuddy]] is acquired by [[Cloud9]]. <ref name="-BnTeT">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/extremumgg/status/1353326850659913728|title=We are ready to show you another way – #OURWAY|date=2021-01-24|author=[[EXTREMUM]]}}</ref><ref name="-Elmapuddy">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Cloud9/status/1353387482868445184|title=Bet you've never seen this coming|date=2021-01-24|author=[[Cloud9]]}}</ref>
* February 4th - [[autimatic]] retires from competitive ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' after being acquired by [[valorant:T1|T1's ''VALORANT'' division]]. <ref name="-autimatic">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/T1/status/1357403550997913601|title=Let's get to work. Welcome @autimaticTV to T1 VALORANT!|date=2021-02-04|author=[[valorant:T1|T1]]}}</ref>

|content4=
* February 21st - '''Gen.G Esports''' announce their return to ''[[Counter-Strike]]'' with the signing of a roster consisting of: [[s1 (Chinese player)|s1]], [[rosar]], [[heartZ]], [[ScreaMy]], [[miracle]], and coach [[KYO]]. <ref name="2024 roster">{{cite web|url=https://weibo.com/6496331561/O1CEk6MLZ|date=2024-02-21|title=Gen.G CS2 2024大名单官宣|trans_title=Gen.G CS2 2024 Roster Official Announcement|language={{Flag|cn}} Simplified Chinese|author='''Gen.G Esports'''}}</ref>
* April 30th - '''Gen.G Esports''' part ways with [[Siyi]] and [[rosar]]. <ref name="-2+2">{{cite web|url=https://www.bilibili.com/opus/979929958646284290|date=2024-04-30|title= Gen.G Esports与Siyi和rosar分道扬镳，并签下Erye和Resay入队|trans_title=Gen.G Esports part ways with Siyi and rosar and sign Erye and Resay |language={{Flag|cn}} Simplified Chinese|author=[[YINXING]]|publisher=[[MythYLHB]]}}</ref>
* May 20th - '''Gen.G Esports''' sign [[Erye]] and [[Resay]]. <ref name="-2+2"/>
* October 21st - '''Gen.G Esports''' disbands. <ref name="gengdisbands">{{cite web|url=https://www.bilibili.com/opus/1053324434261147653|title=Gen.G Esports CS2 disbands|date=2025-02-02|author=[[YINXING]]|publisher=[[MythYLHB]]}}</ref>
}}

